  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be three mutually exclusive events such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. If the maximum and minimum values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to:",
    "image": null
  },
